{"text":"Current whole-outcome correction replacing unclaimed 2b1d287e for simplification audit55563589 / reviewf24d2b56. Builder: check-job retry policy, deadlines, durable per-room concurrency and daily budgets (COST-04,05,13). At current jobs.ts:162-198 dispatch already takes JOB_BATCH=20 with binding/attempt guards. At :477-486 returned refusals mark done; thrown errors are re-owed at +30s without inspecting retryable. checker.ts:93-99,201-205 throws oversized-output with retryable=false. (1) Distinguish returned refusal, typed non-retryable/retryable errors and unknown/lost answers. Honour retryable, stop non-retryable errors with a visible terminal reason, cap attempts with attention and exponential backoff. Unknown remote credential effects remain owned/reconciled even when job retries stop. (2) policy/validate.ts:210-211 accepts positive timeoutSeconds without maximum, checkers/job.ts:155-156 only checks deadline at entry, runner.ts:109-110/sandbox.ts:183-185 default steps to600s. Bound policy timeout and step time by remaining job deadline, abort and clean up at deadline, retain late/duplicate-answer fencing when a new attempt is issued. (3) Add durable per-room concurrency and daily job budgets as explicit policy/deployment settings. Distinguish batch size from active-in-flight capacity; refuse or defer with named reason/resumption. Concurrent dispatch, restart, expiry and late answers cannot double spend or release another attempt's slot. Both deployments use durable_object scheduling: runtime size is supported, max_instances/Wrangler instance_type are not. Retain standard-1 runner sizing and this scheduling policy; any migration needs separate justification/review. Do not infer simultaneous containers or a dollar figure from proposal/alarm counts alone. Historical evidence was at 93a2552e/a6330262; reconcile it against reviewed main 344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482 and credit actual landed fixes. All original functional outcomes remain owed unless explicitly credited. Schedule acts enabling jam first, then only spikes needed by a concrete jam task, then jam and all Artroom docs in parallel (user7363396b/04da4388). This correction adds no blanket before-J2/J3 gate or empty-backlog requirement and commissions no deployment.","body":{"conditions":"Tests distinguish returned refusal from thrown retryable/non-retryable/unknown errors; non-retryable oversized output is not retried; attempt caps/backoff raise attention and preserve remote-effect ownership. Step abort/runner and token cleanup occurs at deadline and oversized policy timeout is bounded. Concurrent/restart/expiry/late-result tests verify durable per-room slots, daily budgets and defer/refuse/resume without duplicate spend. Existing binding/attempt/cleanup guards and supported runtime sizing remain. Provider measurement uses full existing spike-only8bd scope. Root gates and independent exact-head checker review.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8592926f1d4d30e3cf282eadc411dacde51d3ac0 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a3bbf8f3b7ccc7ba4fd596a6bcfe5756d51a77e","target_head":"344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2b1d287e5c0d5acf31930758c6375630d403f1b6","retirement":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e8a10a3771fbd536dbb4f1475452d6f113c1a31c","promise":"absent","completion":"absent"}}